{"name":"Bungalow Brown","hex":"#ad947b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bungalow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A single-storey house, typically with rooms all on one level, or sometimes also with upper rooms set into the roof space.","A thatched or tiled one-story house in India surrounded by a wide veranda; a similar house in this style."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bungalow"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bungalow","blocks":[{"text":"A bungalow is a small house or cottage that is typically single- or one-and-a-half-storey. If a smaller upper storey exists, then it is frequently set in the roof and windows that come out from the roof. It may be surrounded by wide verandas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/149MyrtleReedsburgWI.JPG/330px-149MyrtleReedsburgWI.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bungalow","wikidata":"Q850107"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/StateLibQld_2_228966_Home_Building_Publishing_Company_home%2C_Design_No._3%2C_1939.jpg/500px-StateLibQld_2_228966_Home_